# What Nix calls the things profiles ask for.
#
# A sixth vocabulary, and the shortest: Nix package names are almost
# always the upstream project name, so only the ones that differ are
# worth writing down.
#
# Reading a source's packages without its aliases loads the
# components and offers none of them, which looks exactly like the
# source being empty. That has happened three times now, once per
# source added.

Capability: window-manager
Resolves-To: hyprland | sway | i3 | river | bspwm | dwm

Capability: terminal-emulator
Resolves-To: foot | alacritty | kitty | wezterm | ghostty

Capability: text-editor
Resolves-To: neovim | vim | helix | nano

Capability: code-editor
Resolves-To: vscode | vscodium | zed-editor

Capability: web-browser
Resolves-To: firefox | chromium | brave

Capability: status-bar
Resolves-To: waybar | polybar | eww

Capability: application-launcher
Resolves-To: fuzzel | rofi | wofi | dmenu | anyrun

Capability: notification-daemon
Resolves-To: mako | dunst | swaynotificationcenter

Capability: screen-locker
Resolves-To: hyprlock | swaylock | i3lock

Capability: wallpaper-setter
Resolves-To: hyprpaper | swaybg | feh

Capability: file-manager
Resolves-To: nautilus | dolphin | thunar | yazi | ranger

Capability: terminal-multiplexer
Resolves-To: tmux | zellij

Capability: fuzzy-finder
Resolves-To: fzf | skim

Capability: modern-shell
Resolves-To: fish | zsh | nushell

Capability: network-scanner
Resolves-To: nmap

Capability: packet-analyser
Resolves-To: wireshark | tcpdump | termshark

Capability: compiler-toolchain
Resolves-To: gcc | clang

Capability: video-player
Resolves-To: mpv | vlc

Capability: image-editor
Resolves-To: gimp | krita | inkscape
